{"id":"tour-divide","title":"Tour Divide (Great Divide Route)","who":"Classic bikepacking route; race since 2008","when":"Since 2008","vehicle":"Mountain or gravel bike","kind":"bike","color":"#15803d","summary":"About 4,400 km of mostly gravel along the Rocky Mountains, from Banff in Canada to the Mexican border, crossing the Continental Divide again and again. The world's best-known bikepacking route: the race record is under two weeks; most riders take two months.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Tour Divide","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tour_Divide"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Great Divide Mountain Bike Route","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Divide_Mountain_Bike_Route"}],"approximate":"Towns on the route; the line between them follows roads, not the exact gravel tracks (use the official maps to ride it).","km":3919,"bbox":[-116.1517,31.333,-105.8743,51.2652],"stops":[{"name":"Banff","place":"Banff, Alberta","at":[51.1751,-115.5721],"text":"The start in the Canadian Rockies, in June, often with snow still on the passes.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Town_of_Banff_viewed_from_Sulphur_Mountain.jpg/500px-Town_of_Banff_viewed_from_Sulphur_Mountain.jpg","page":"Banff, Alberta","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Town_of_Banff_viewed_from_Sulphur_Mountain.jpg","credit":"Ethan Sahagun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Elkford","place":"Elkford, British Columbia","at":[50.0245,-114.9218],"text":"Remote forest roads in grizzly country."},{"name":"Fernie","place":"Fernie, British Columbia","at":[49.5042,-115.0629],"text":"A mountain town before the US border.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Fernie_BC_-_downtown_looking_south.jpg/500px-Fernie_BC_-_downtown_looking_south.jpg","page":"Fernie, British Columbia","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fernie_BC_-_downtown_looking_south.jpg","credit":"waferboard","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Eureka","place":"Eureka, Montana","at":[48.88,-115.0535],"text":"Into Montana at the Roosville crossing.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Eureka_Montana_Downtown_Looking_Northwest.jpg/500px-Eureka_Montana_Downtown_Looking_Northwest.jpg","page":"Eureka, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eureka_Montana_Downtown_Looking_Northwest.jpg","credit":"Royalbroil","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Whitefish","place":"Whitefish, Montana","at":[48.4108,-114.3346],"text":"Near Glacier National Park.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Downtown-whitefish-2006.jpg/500px-Downtown-whitefish-2006.jpg","page":"Whitefish, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown-whitefish-2006.jpg","credit":"WikiCapa at English Wikipedia","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Seeley Lake","place":"Seeley Lake, Montana","at":[47.1553,-113.4484],"text":"Lakes and forest tracks south.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Seeley_Lake_Montana_20130716_04.JPG/500px-Seeley_Lake_Montana_20130716_04.JPG","page":"Seeley Lake, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seeley_Lake_Montana_20130716_04.JPG","credit":"Djembayz","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Helena","place":"Helena, Montana","at":[46.5927,-112.0363],"text":"Montana's capital, after big climbs.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Montana_State_Capitol_by_T._Elizabeth.jpg/500px-Montana_State_Capitol_by_T._Elizabeth.jpg","page":"Helena, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montana_State_Capitol_by_T._Elizabeth.jpg","credit":"Tracey Elizabeth","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Butte","place":"Butte, Montana","at":[46.0132,-112.5365],"text":"An old mining town on the Divide.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Butte_uptown.jpg/500px-Butte_uptown.jpg","page":"Butte, Montana","